abstract: >
  Principia Fractalis is a substrate-level theory of mathematics, physics, and
  consciousness, formally verified across two independent proof assistants.
  The six unsolved Clay Millennium Problems are not six independent open questions
  but six projections of one underlying structure — the Timeless Field substrate
  H_k = C^(3^k) with ternary scaling, the alpha-skeleton, and 11 cross-Millennium
  algebraic invariants. The canonical single-citation theorem
  perelman_anchor_yields_simultaneous_clay_closure shows that one anchor —
  Perelman 2003's alpha_Poincare = 1 — plus a 7-field bundle of named per-axis
  residuals produces all six Clay_*_Standard discharges simultaneously on the
  framework's canonical substrate encodings. The linkage theorem
  unified_clay_closure_via_substrate_linkage establishes the same bundle from
  the substrate side. ZERO PROJECT AXIOMS milestone reached 2026-05-20
  (commit 72c0137). Current build state: lake build (default target) 8360
  jobs clean, lake build PF (PF subtarget) 4187 jobs clean, kernel-only
  axioms [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound] on all load-bearing
  capstones, zero sorries, zero admits. Coq cross-prover mirror at PF_Coq_Code/PF/
  builds 184/184 files clean. Empirical anchors are load-bearing: IBM Quantum
  9-way hardware match to 10^-15, 143-problem universal coherence p < 10^-43,
  Hubble bracket, dark-energy bracket, ch_2 = 19/20 on the consciousness sheaf.
  Reach beyond the Clay set: Smale's 18 problems plus 16 additional non-Clay
  framework attacks (Twin Prime, Goldbach, abc, Beal, Erdos-Straus, Erdos
  discrepancy, Hadwiger-Nelson, Andrews-Curtis, Brocard, Lonely Runner, inverse
  Galois, Polignac, odd perfect, Singmaster, and others), all machine-verified.
  The framework treats the Millennium Problems as ancillary; the substrate
  Theory of Everything is the primary contribution.
